body:
Greg's direction (2026-10-18 21:20Z, via Engram::Advisor #1189, relayed by Fable2 in TermAl mailbox 4daa5b87 #2576), verbatim: 'Merger should batch 2–3 independent ready changes per integration instead of serial single-item landings. Select disjoint paths/no ordering dependency, carry each onto the same current master, resolve any actual conflict, then run one gate/review on the exact combined freeze. Keep conflicting/dependent changes separate. Make batch fan-in the default at next boundary.'

Integration-owner (Opus2) pre-push checks for a batch:
- fast-forward, with origin equal to the base;
- the commit tree equals the combined freeze, and the index and diff hashes equal the one combined gate input, with a stable fingerprint;
- one review pair on the combined freeze (a member's earlier pair counts only for a byte-exact disjoint carry under the coordinator's ruling);
- per member, a fresh passing evaluation, with done after the push;
- pairwise path disjointness checked by me; hold on any overlap not ruled on;
- carriage-return, authority-text and body-id checks;
- one release build and install (plus ui/dist if any member touches ui/).

Added landing checks (2026-10-19, from Fable2 #2582 and #2588; they apply to single landings too):
(a) Greg's merger-role rule: "Merger integrates/freeze/gate/review/landing only; every defect, including one-line test/fixture/doc fix, returns to an owning coder in its own worktree." The integration owner writes no fixes. Refuse a landing whose tree carries a merger-authored delta: each member's committed blobs must equal its reviewed tree, or, in shared files, carry only its own reviewed +/- lines.
(b) Known gap w-5cc74b7d7166: a delegated reviewer spawned with cwd at a .tmp worktree gets workdir = the MAIN checkout. A counted review must show reads of the frozen input (the named root's absolute paths, `git show <tree>:<path>`, or that root's diff). A review that read only main-checkout copies does not count.
(c) A gate on unstaged or untracked input (the index equals the base index): rebuild the launcher fields from the commit with .tmp/fp-recon.mjs (args: BASE COMMIT RUN_DIR), using scripts/review-freeze-fingerprint.mjs definitions. The composite must equal the gate's expected fingerprint.
